    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Iconic riverside residence on c.0.7 Acre"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Iconic riverside residence on c.0.7 Acre"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Tuck Mill is a fully restored traditional residence extending to c.1,488sqft.\r\n\r\nThis original Mill Building has been completely transformed and painstakingly restored into a strikingly beautiful residence with a selection of outbuildings including a garage, workshop, and out-buildings all on a lush c.0.7 Acre plot running down to the adjoining Argideen River.\r\n\r\nExternally the house takes the form of a traditional farmhouse which has been transformed into a bright, airy and characterful home complete with all the modern conveniences and comforts.\r\n\r\nThe result of careful design, each of the rooms enjoys the Western facing front, overlooking the sun terrace and gardens below.\r\n\r\nInternal accommodation is contemporary with warm and spacious rooms throughout.\r\n\r\nA newly installed kitchen having desirable dual aspect windows is the heart of the home and flows seamlessly into the central sitting room with its brick surrounded solid fuel stove and original timber beam the focal point of the ground floor. A door to the sun terrace from this room brings the outside in during the warm summer months and is a beautiful yet simple feature adding to the attraction.\r\n\r\nA separate and sizable lounge with its restored cast-iron fireplace completes the ground floor accommodation.\r\n\r\nOn the half landing are the airing cupboard and family bathroom with its Italian marble surrounded jacuzzi bath.\r\n\r\nOn the first floor, 3 of the 4 bedrooms are double with the master being ensuite and all having been newly carpeted.\r\n\r\nThe outbuildings feature a collection of buildings each with power, lighting and electric roller doors. The largest being the garage with a workshop and utility room to the side along with an office overhead.\r\n\r\nAt the other end of the house is another workshop with loft and storage room.\r\n\r\nBelow these is the garden/music room, a raised area with composite decking platform overlooking the gardens and forming part of the old mill building.\r\n\r\nThe gardens have been maturing into a multi-color oasis with the huge pond at the centre of the show having wildlife visitors throughout the year enjoying the peaceful surroundings of this organic habitat.\r\n\r\nTuck Mill is a truly special place, rarely seen and impossible to recreate. Its proximity to a selection of towns, schools, beaches and less than an hour to Cork City & Airport make it an attractive convenient property with a unique allure.\r\n\r\nServices: Broadband, Electricity, Private Water, Private Drainage."
      },
